 Visualize Your Data
 ===================

 The advent of graphical programming and GUIs mean the days of bland statistical 
 reports and simple data representation are a thing of the past.  Windows 
 applications demand your programs be as visual as possible.  Essential Graphics 
 Chart for Windows gives you the functionality you need to visualize your data 
 in the Windows environment.
 
 
 Designed To Do The Job
 ======================

 Chart for Windows provides all the functionality you need to add professional 
 charts to your Windows applications.  All charts are implemented through DLLs 
 enabling multiple charts to be displayed in any number of windows simultaneously.  
 Another benefit of the DLL implementation is that you can use the Chart library 
 with any Windows API compatible language, such as C/C++.  A powerful interactive 
 CASE tool is also provided for designing and prototyping charts.  
 
 
 Feature Rich, Programmer Friendly
 =================================
 
 A wide selection of chart types and configuration settings is available in 
 Chart For Windows.  All of this is provided without requiring extensive coding.  
 Available charts such as 2-D and 3-D bars and pies, line and scatter, 
 high-low-close, real time, area, pyramid and more can be displayed with less 
 than 10 additional lines of Windows code.  Default information is implemented 
 for all chart settings which allows you to display your data in only a few 
 function calls.
 
 The variety and flexibility of our chart types allows your program to give a 
 new perspective to its data.  EG Chart for Windows gives you complete control 
 over all presentation aspects of the charts through the use of "message based" 
 function calls.  Titles, colors, labels, fonts, legends and other options are 
 all easily configurable.  

 Our CASE tool enables you to interactively develop charts which can be stored 
 to disk and recalled later for display in your application.
 
 Visual representation is only one part of a complete graphics presentation.  
 Printer output is handled by Chart for Windows through the use of a virtual 
 bitmap driver.  This enables you to produce professional hardcopy output on 
 any graphics printer supported by Windows.
 
 Software Backed By Professionals
 ================================
 
 South Mountain Software has been producing quality programming tools for over 
 eight years.  Our graphics libraries for DOS have been used by over 7,000 
 programmers worldwide in a variety of applications.  This commitment to quality 
 and support now stands behind Chart For Windows.  Let Chart for Windows open a 
 window of opportunity to visualize your data.
 
                                  ================
                                      Features  
                                  ================

                * No royalties or runtime fees
                * Charts may be displayed in the parent window or located in
                  windows of their own
                * 2-D bar, stacked bar, pie, line, scatter, hi-low-close, 
                  pyramid and area charts
                * 3-D bar, stacked bar, pie, pyramid and area charts
                * True perspective and rotational capability on 3-D charts
                * Real time charts with scrolling horizontal axis and data values
                * Legends for all chart types
                * Integer, long, float or double data values
                * CASE tool to supplement chart development
                * Virtual bitmapped output to a any graphics Windows printer
                * Plenty of example programs
